# Code Style Guidelines

## Naming (C#)

- Types, methods, properties, public fields: `PascalCase`
- Locals, parameters, private fields: `_camelCase` for fields when that matches surrounding code; otherwise match the file
- Constants: `PascalCase` or `UPPER_SNAKE` only where already used nearby
- Files: one primary type per file, `PascalCase` matching the type (`FileService.cs`)
- XAML: views `*View.axaml`, pair with code-behind; ViewModels `*ViewModel.cs`

## Language settings

- Target `net10.0` with nullable reference types enabled
- Prefer pattern matching and early returns over deep nesting
- Avoid drive-by refactors; match existing formatting and CommunityToolkit.Mvvm patterns (`[ObservableProperty]`, `[RelayCommand]`)

## Documentation

- XML docs only where public APIs are non-obvious or shared across assemblies
- Prefer clear names over comments; comment non-obvious encoding/EOL/LSP edge cases

## Error handling

- Catch at UI / command boundaries; log unexpected failures to `%APPDATA%/XPad/crash.log`
- Prefer user-visible, non-fatal messages over process termination
- Do not swallow encoding or file-watcher errors silently without a status/path for the user

## Avalonia / editor specifics

- Do not bind multi-megabyte text as a two-way string; use `TextDocument`
- Prefer existing theme resources; preserve Dark / Light / System / Monokai / Hacker / AMOLED / GitHub
- PowerShell scripts: Windows-friendly cmdlets (`Get-ChildItem`, etc.); write complex content with file tools, not fragile redirection

## Scripts & packaging

- Publish / MSIX / release live under `scripts/` — extend them rather than inventing parallel pipelines
- Keep `package.json` + `scripts/xpad.js` only as the Bun/npm launcher to Release `xpad.exe`

